Subject: observe executed terminal word input ranges
Upstream-Status: Local embedding (not submitted)

Expose one synchronous word invocation and its actually consumed input-byte
interval on terminal collector events. The existing pos/end fields remain
terminal buffer coordinates. Plain text is reported one input byte per logical
glyph; an escape's full consumed source interval accompanies every glyph it
emits. The observer cannot alter formatting and may not retain the borrowed
word pointer beyond the callback. This is private provenance for bounded
compatible-reference annotation, not an authored file coordinate.

